**Day 45: Flask – Connecting to MySQL**  

**Topic:**  
Connecting a Flask application to a MySQL database using the `mysql-connector-python` library. Executing SQL queries from Flask, fetching data, and displaying it on a web page. Practical implementation includes connecting to VolyoDB and displaying an employee list.  

**Learning Objectives:**  
• Understand how to integrate Flask with MySQL using `mysql-connector-python`.  
• Learn to execute SQL queries within a Flask application.  
• Fetch and display database records dynamically on a web page.  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  
• Set up a Flask application with MySQL connectivity.  
• Write and execute SQL queries to retrieve employee data from VolyoDB.  
• Create a web page to display the fetched employee list.  

**Important Concepts:**  
• Database connection pooling in Flask for efficient MySQL interactions.  
• Parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection vulnerabilities.  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  
• `SELECT * FROM employees;`  
• `cursor.execute(query)` and `cursor.fetchall()` for data retrieval.  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  
• Building internal dashboards to display real-time employee data.  
• Developing dynamic web applications with backend database interactions.  

**Tools / Tech:**  
• Flask (Python web framework)  
• `mysql-connector-python` (MySQL database driver)  
• MySQL (VolyoDB as the target database)  

**Summary:**  
Learned to connect Flask with MySQL, execute queries, and dynamically display data on a web page. Gained hands-on experience in integrating backend databases with web applications, a critical skill for full-stack development.  

